f 1043 #edb/ref 17592186093326 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092460 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092460 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line Using Differentiation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092460 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186093324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092460 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092460 #edb/ref 1050 600.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092460 #edb/ref 1050 600.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186092460 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "708c0aaf-266b-5a9d-b352-10ed7b4b2883" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093324 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186093325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093324 #edb/ref 1061 657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093324 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4a6af753-c85c-59f9-be67-03ca672b3493" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093324 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186093430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093325 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186093326 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093325 #edb/ref 1061 658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093325 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dabdab57-40b6-5940-8089-29b4010d85ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093325 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093326 #edb/ref 1061 663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093326 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "53c42827-7f73-5fef-997e-9f666fc35841" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093326 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093430 #edb/ref 1064 "The equation of the tangent line to the curve $y = f(x)$ at the point $P(x_1,y_1),$ in point-slope form, is given by\n\n$$\ny - y_1 = m (x - x_1), \\hspace{.75cm} m=f'(x_1).\n$$\n\nHere, $m = f'(x_1)$ because $f'(x_1)$ represents the slope of the tangent line to $y=f(x)$ at the point $(x_1,y_1).$\n\nFor example, suppose we want to compute the equation of the tangent line to the curve $y=x^2$ at the point $P(1,1).$\n\n![](images/48/487d21289b468fb82efa2097e425dd560811dc3165890509dacbab8093e0ecdb.png)\n\nSince $y=x^2,$ we have $f(x)=x^2.$ We begin by calculating the derivative of $f(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nf'(x) \t\t = \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(x^2)= 2x\n$$\n\nThen, we determine the slope of the tangent at $P(1,1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nm = f'(1)  = 2(1) = 2\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we substitute the slope $m=2$ and the coordinates of $P(1,1)$ into the point-slope form, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-1 & =2(x-1) \\\\ y & =2x-2+1 \\\\ y & =2x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is $y=2x-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093430 #edb/ref 1065 354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093430 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8b0ed179-00e3-5e1a-84fc-c78773cfef19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093430 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241815 #edb/ref 1080 "y=16x-8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241815 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241815 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "462f21c8-a32c-5cda-84b7-37744e22718b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241859 #edb/ref 1080 "y=5x-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241859 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241859 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b650713-54c4-53ad-9158-64cadb27ca27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241970 #edb/ref 1080 "y=16x-12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241970 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241970 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5726209a-7467-583c-a028-1f93390b638f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186242665 #edb/ref 1080 "y=5x-13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186242665 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186242665 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a96129cb-4819-5b81-9f60-2fc2160dba34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243151 #edb/ref 1080 "y=x-12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243151 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243151 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dda5ca10-115e-5